    "owner": "R20",
    "policy": "Box3D worker tasks run on the pool the application root passes to CreateParallelEnvironment; in products that is the engine compute pool (CmpJob, g_pThreadPool). A parallel environment may use at most the pool's threads plus the calling thread, so physics adds no threads and the CmpJob capacity row in quality/budgets/scheduler-v1.json (3 on the Linux desktop unless -threads) is the physics worker budget: at most 4 workers by default. The benchmark host starts a private pool with workers - 1 threads, so its 8-worker rows model a -threads 8 configuration."
